otism just is patriotism we can  debate whether so-called Patriot doesn't  make sense you can have a serious  conversation about is there any sense in  being proud of where you by mere chance  happy  to be born that's a debate but where we  really can't debate is the reality that  patriotism and nationalism are two  different things if we list patriotic  leaders in in history we could say we'll  listen Franklin Delano Roosevelt was a  patriotic leader the New Deal Social  Security managing the post Great  Depression era patriotism who were  nationalist leaders of Notepad Ataturk  Ho Chi Minh Hitler kim ill sung from  North Korea Mussolini Gaddafi in Libya  this is not great company but it is  Trump's company Trump calling himself a  nationalist has meaning and I'm curious  who told him to start using this word if  I had to guess I would say Stephen  Miller was probably a factor in Trump  coming out and saying I am a nationalist  I typically don't buy into the idea that  Trump is playing three-dimensional chess  now but I think he is in this case  because well it comes across as him just  saying that he's a patriot by how he  worded it in the context of that video  calling himself a nationalist but it's  also a dog whistle right it serves to  you know bring out that base of  supporters who are white nationalist the  people like Richard Spencer and Miley  innopolis and those type of people who  voted for him well Anthony scaramouche  II one of the many former White House  communications directors he says that it  is a sort of dog whistle but it is not  to rile up the right that it's to anger  the left that it's a sort of trolling  take a look at what Anthony scaramouche  II had to say about this in the--  scaramouche you are you a nationalist no  I'm not a nationalist no he's he's not a  nationalist I mean he's saying that he's  a nationalist cuz he wants you to be  upset about it but he's really not a  nationalist I mean if you really  understand the historical word 